      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To analyze the causes of pain after total knee arthroplasty (TKA), and to review its diagnosis and treatment methods."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "Domestic and abroad literature concerning pain after TKA was extensively reviewed and thoroughly analyzed."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Pain after TKA was divided into intra-articular and extra-articular factors, systematic assessment, appropriate imaging, and laboratory tests were useful to confirm the diagnosis; targeted surgery could effectively relieve the pain."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The causes of pain after TKA are complex and diverse, the first step is to exclude intraarticular infection, for patients having a clear cause the appropriate surgery is effective. Otherwise revision should be carried out cautiously under condition of unexplained pain and conservative treatment can relieve pain to some degree."
        }
      ]},
